   228	### 4.0.1 — Loop-engineering rules (LE-N), in plain English
   229	
   230	The `LE-N` tags cited inline in the phases below are shorthand for these rules (from the
   231	loop-engineering work). The tag is only a reference id; the rule text is what binds.
   232	
   233	- **LE-1 — Refutation-default review.** A reviewer assumes the implementation is wrong and records concrete attempts to break each acceptance criterion; a "no findings" review counts only with refutation attempts shown.
   234	- **LE-2 — Driver auto-advance.** A deterministic driver may advance mechanical phase transitions; it never authors participant content or decides contested issues.
   235	- **LE-3 — Model diversity.** A reviewer sharing the implementer's model is likelier to rubber-stamp; `require_model_diversity: true` turns an all-shared-model reviewer set into a hard gate.
   236	- **LE-4 — Verification command.** `checks:` in `00-prompt.md` is the build/test gate the driver runs (as `sh -c`) at Phase 5/8.
   237	- **LE-5 — Loop budgets.** Driver runs are bounded by max steps / wall-clock / cost.
   238	- **LE-7 / LE-11 — Close-decision integrity.** Before an auto-driven close, a goal-done check verifies FINAL's observable acceptance criteria; reservations or too-few reviewers escalate rather than close.
   239	- **LE-10 — Candidate remediation.** Remediation ideas may start as `status: candidate`.
   240	
   241	### Phase 0 — Kickoff
   242	
   243	The agent (or user) who starts the idea creates `ideas/<slug>/00-prompt.md`:
   244	
   245	    ---

