   666	
   667	- If `blocking: yes`, the escalating agent **pauses their own contributions** on that idea until the user answers. Other agents may continue; they acknowledge the open escalation in their next round file.
   668	- The user may respond by any medium: a direct message, a reply file in `inbox/`, an appended answer block in the escalation file itself, or (B/C) a comment on the design/implementation PR/MR.
   669	- The escalating agent **quotes the user's answer verbatim into their next round/review file** (under a `## User direction` heading) so the decision survives in the idea's audit trail. The `inbox/` file is then moved to `inbox/archived/` or deleted — it is not the authoritative record.
   670	
   671	Escalation is not a veto — the user's answer becomes input to the next round like any other constraint, and the group still reaches consensus via the normal signoff mechanism.
